  "prompt": "[system]\nYou generate executable, reliable VRP metaheuristics for evolutionary search.\n\n[user]\nSTRATEGY m3_simplify_generalize: Create a simpler and more robust version of one parent by removing brittle, over-specialized, redundant, or overly complex components. Preserve the essential idea and required behavior while improving generalization and maintainability.\n\nUse the provided parents as the primary source of design changes.\n\nIncorporate, adapt, recombine, repair, or refine the listed parents.\n\nDo not ignore the parents or generate an unrelated solver from scratch.\n\nVRP objective: lower maximum route distance across trucks is better. Feasibility is mandatory.\n\nPARENTS:\nCandidate cand_000022: simulated_annealing_vrp\nStatus: valid; gap: 18.7113\nThought: Multi-start nearest-neighbor with DP split, improved by Simulated Annealing using 2-opt, relocate, and exchange operators. Random restarts with deterministic seed for reproducibility. Accepts worse solutions probabilistically to escape local optima.\nMean gap: 18.711347856327336\nMean max route distance: 2.4298797827246266\nMean total route distance: 14.183996155319846\nGap by instance size: {'100': 18.711347856327336}\nGap by truck count: {'6': 18.711347856327336}\nHistory source: yes\nHistory bucket: vrp:size:100\nHistory role: regime specialist\nCode:\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport random\nimport math\n\ndef solve_vrp(distance_matrix: np.ndarray, truck_count: int) -> list[list[int]]:\n    n = distance_matrix.shape[0]\n    customers = list(range(1, n))\n    random.seed(0)\n    np.random.seed(0)\n    \n    best_routes = None\n    best_max = float('inf')\n    \n    def route_distance(route):\n        if len(route) < 2:\n            return 0.0\n        total = 0.0\n        for i in range(len(route)-1):\n            total += distance_matrix[route[i]][route[i+1]]\n        return total\n    \n    def compute_max(routes):\n        return max(route_distance(r) for r in routes)\n    \n    def build_initial(start):\n        # Nearest neighbor giant tour from start\n        giant_path = [start]\n        remaining = set(customers)\n        remaining.remove(start)\n        current = start\n        while remaining:\n            nearest = None\n            min_dist = float('inf')\n            for c in remaining:\n                d = distance_matrix[current][c]\n                if d < min_dist or (d == min_dist and c < nearest):\n                    min_dist = d\n                    nearest = c\n            giant_path.append(nearest)\n            remaining.remove(nearest)\n            current = nearest\n        # DP split\n        L = len(giant_path)\n        if L < truck_count:\n            routes = []\n            idx = 0\n            for t in range(truck_count):\n                if idx < L:\n                    route = [0, giant_path[idx], 0]\n                    idx += 1\n                else:\n                    route = [0, 0]\n                routes.append(route)\n            return routes\n        dist0_to = [distance_matrix[0][c] for c in giant_path]\n        dist_to0 = [distance_matrix[c][0] for c in giant_path]\n        edge = [distance_matrix[giant_path[i]][giant_path[i+1]] for i in range(L-1)]\n        pref = [0]*L\n        for i in range(1, L):\n            pref[i] = pref[i-1] + edge[i-1]\n        def seg_cost(i, j):\n            return dist0_to[i] + (pref[j] - pref[i]) + dist_to0[j]\n        INF = 1e18\n        dp = [[INF]*(L+1) for _ in range(truck_count+1)]\n        prev = [[-1]*(L+1) for _ in range(truck_count+1)]\n        dp[0][0] = 0\n        for k in range(1, truck_count+1):\n            for i in range(k, L+1):\n                best_val = INF\n                best_j = -1\n                for j in range(k-1, i):\n                    if dp[k-1][j] < INF:\n                        seg = seg_cost(j, i-1)\n                        candidate = max(dp[k-1][j], seg)\n                        if candidate < best_val:\n                            best_val = candidate\n                            best_j = j\n                dp[k][i] = best_val\n                prev[k][i] = best_j\n        if dp[truck_count][L] == INF:\n            return None\n        split_points = []\n        k = truck_count\n        i = L\n        while k > 0 and i > 0:\n            j = prev[k][i]\n            split_points.append(j)\n            i = j\n            k -= 1\n        split_points.reverse()\n        split_points.append(L)\n        routes = []\n        for r in range(truck_count):\n            start_idx = split_points[r]\n            end_idx = split_points[r+1]\n            rc = giant_path[start_idx:end_idx]\n            if not rc:\n                route = [0,0]\n            else:\n                route = [0] + rc + [0]\n            routes.append(route)\n        while len(routes) < truck_count:\n            routes.append([0,0])\n        return routes\n    \n    def local_search_sa(routes, max_iter):\n        current_routes = [list(r) for r in routes]\n        current_max = compute_max(current_routes)\n        best_routes = [list(r) for r in current_routes]\n        best_max = current_max\n        # Initial temperature proportional to current_max\n        T = current_max * 0.5\n        T_min = 1e-6\n        cooling = max_iter / ( (T - T_min) if T - T_min > 0 else 1 )\n        \n        for iteration in range(max_iter):\n            new_routes = [list(r) for r in current_routes]\n            # Choose operator randomly\n            op = random.choice(['2opt', 'relocate', 'exchange'])\n            if op == '2opt':\n                # Intra-route 2-opt on random route\n                r_idx = random.randrange(truck_count)\n                route = new_routes[r_idx]\n                if len(route) <= 3:\n                    continue\n                i = random.randrange(1, len(route)-2)\n                j = random.randrange(i+1, len(route)-1)\n                new_route = route[:i] + route[i:j+1][::-1] + route[j+1:]\n                new_routes[r_idx] = new_route\n            elif op == 'relocate':\n                # Move a customer from longest route to another\n                dists = [route_distance(r) for r in new_routes]\n                longest_idx = max(range(truck_count), key=lambda x: dists[x])\n                other_indices = [i for i in range(truck_count) if i != longest_idx]\n                if not other_indices:\n                    continue\n                from_route = new_routes[longest_idx]\n                if len(from_route) <= 2:\n                    continue\n                cust_pos = random.randrange(1, len(from_route)-1)\n                cust = from_route[cust_pos]\n                to_idx = random.choice(other_indices)\n                to_route = new_routes[to_idx]\n                pos = random.randrange(1, len(to_route))\n                # Remove cust from from_route\n                new_from = from_route[:cust_pos] + from_route[cust_pos+1:]\n                if len(new_from) == 1:\n                    new_from = [0,0]\n                # Insert into to_route\n                new_to = to_route[:pos] + [cust] + to_route[pos:]\n                new_routes[longest_idx] = new_from\n                new_routes[to_idx] = new_to\n            else: # exchange\n                r1 = random.randrange(truck_count)\n                r2 = random.randrange(truck_count)\n                if r1 == r2:\n                    continue\n                route1 = new_routes[r1]\n                route2 = new_routes[r2]\n                if len(route1) <= 2 or len(route2) <= 2:\n                    continue\n                pos1 = random.randrange(1, len(route1)-1)\n                pos2 = random.randrange(1, len(route2)-1)\n                cust1 = route1[pos1]\n                cust2 = route2[pos2]\n                new_route1 = list(route1)\n                new_route2 = list(route2)\n                new_route1[pos1] = cust2\n                new_route2[pos2] = cust1\n                new_routes[r1] = new_route1\n                new_routes[r2] = new_route2\n            \n            new_max = compute_max(new_routes)\n            delta = new_max - current_max\n            if delta < 0 or random.random() < math.exp(-delta / T):\n                current_routes = new_routes\n                current_max = new_max\n                if current_max < best_max:\n                    best_routes = [list(r) for r in current_routes]\n                    best_max = current_max\n                    try:\n                        report_best_vrp(best_routes)\n                    except:\n                        pass\n            # Cool down\n            T = max(T_min, T - cooling)\n        return best_routes\n    \n    num_restarts = min(10, n)\n    for restart in range(num_restarts):\n        if restart == 0:\n            start = 1  # deterministic start\n        else:\n            start = random.choice(customers)\n        routes = build_initial(start)\n        if routes is None:\n            continue\n        # Improve with SA\n        max_iter = n * 2\n        improved_routes = local_search_sa(routes, max_iter)\n        cur_max = compute_max(improved_routes)\n        if cur_max < best_max - 1e-10:\n            best_routes = improved_routes\n            best_max = cur_max\n            try:\n                report_best_vrp(best_routes)\n            except:\n                pass\n    \n    return best_routes\n```\n\nImplement exactly this interface:\n\ndef solve_vrp(\n    distance_matrix: np.ndarray,  # (n, n), depot is node 0\n    truck_count: int,\n) -> list[list[int]]:\n\nRules:\n- VRP is a static multi-truck routing problem; the objective is to minimize the maximum route distance across trucks.\n- Return exactly truck_count routes.\n- Each route must start at depot node 0 and end at depot node 0.\n- Every customer node 1..n-1 must appear exactly once across all routes.\n- An unused truck route must be [0, 0].\n- Use only distance_matrix; do not assume coordinates, instance size, truck 